[32m+[m[32m# API Health Monitoring[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA React/Vite dashboard backed by an Express server, SQLite, and a server-side monitoring worker. Enabled monitors continue checking while the browser is closed because the worker runs in the backend process.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Install dependencies:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32m   npm install[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and set a long local `JWT_SECRET`. Keep `.env` private and never commit it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Initialize the database without deleting existing data:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32m   npm run db:init[m
[32m+[m[32m   ```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Run[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen two VS Code terminals in the project root.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBackend:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run server[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFrontend:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run dev[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen `http://localhost:5173`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe backend resumes enabled monitors on startup. Stop the backend with Ctrl+C only after checks are complete.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Email alerts[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDevelopment uses `EMAIL_PROVIDER=console`, which records notification history and prints a Nodemailer JSON preview without contacting a provider.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor Resend, set `EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend`, set `RESEND_API_KEY` in the backend-only `.env`, and set `EMAIL_FROM` to a sender/domain verified in Resend. The server sends `POST https://api.resend.com/emails` directly from Node using the key; the key is never included in Vite variables or API responses. `ALERT_TO_EMAIL` is not used for monitor notifications because each alert must go to the owning user's account email.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mResend setup:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Verify a sending domain or sender in the Resend dashboard.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Create a Resend API key and put it only in the root `.env` as `RESEND_API_KEY`.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Set `EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend` and `EMAIL_FROM` to the verified sender.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Restart `npm run server`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe backend validates these settings at startup. It records an alert as sent only when Resend returns a successful response containing an email ID. Without a real key and verified sender, use console mode; real delivery has not been tested by this project setup.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor real delivery, set `EMAIL_PROVIDER=smtp` and configure these variables in `.env`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `SMTP_HOST`: your provider's SMTP hostname[m
[32m+[m[32m- `SMTP_PORT`: commonly `587` for STARTTLS or `465` for implicit TLS[m
[32m+[m[32m- `SMTP_SECURE`: `false` for STARTTLS on 587, `true` for 465[m
[32m+[m[32m- `SMTP_USER`: the provider account or mailbox[m
[32m+[m[32m- `SMTP_PASS`: an app password or provider-specific SMTP credential, never a normal account password when the provider supports app passwords[m
[32m+[m[32m- `EMAIL_FROM`: a verified sender address[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe server refuses to start in SMTP mode if required settings are missing. It does not log credential values. An alert is recorded as sent only after Nodemailer reports the recipient as accepted.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Checks[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run db:init[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run build[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm test[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe test suite uses local HTTP servers and a temporary SQLite database. It does not call or overload external APIs.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## API verification[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mInvoke-RestMethod http://localhost:5000/api/health[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExpected response:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```json[m
[32m+[m[32m{"ok":true}[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
